# Space Engineers warships v{{VERSION}} ({{VARIANT}})

{{INTRO}}

Package contents: {{COUNTS}}. **No DLC blocks.** The Shrike and Corsair are small-grid ships, the Warden and Leviathan are large-grid ships. All of them can be flown by hand
from their seat and fly and fight by themselves when nobody sits in it. Nothing in this package has been tried in the game yet: it was built and tested in a simulator
(see "What was tested" below, and do the in-game tests at the end first).

| Ship | Class | Grid | Programmable Blocks | Drones |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Shrike** | fighter, 1 pilot, 17 m | small | `[Helm] Shrike` | none |
| **Corsair** | corvette, 36 m | small | `[Helm] Corsair`, `[Staff] Corsair`, `[Bay] Corsair` | 2 cradles in the outrigger pylons (`Corsair Wing` = with two Hornets) |
| **Warden** | frigate, 85 m | large | `[Helm][SH] Warden Helm`, `[Staff][SH] Warden Staff`, `[Pod] Pod PB` (on the docked pod) | one docked 4-slot pod (`Warden Wing` = with four Hornets) |
| **Leviathan** | dreadnought, 222 m | large | `[Helm][SH] Leviathan Helm`, `[Staff][SH] Leviathan Staff`, `[Pod] Pod PB 1` and `2` (on the two docked pods) | two docked 4-slot pods (`Leviathan Wing` = with eight Hornets) |
| **Cradle Pod** | empty 4-slot drone pod | small | `[Pod] Pod PB` | docks into a Warden / Leviathan hangar |

## Install

1. Unzip this package anywhere. You get `Blueprints/<Name>/{bp.sbc,thumb.png}`, `Scripts/*.cs` and this README. The scripts in `Scripts/` are compacted (no comments) so that they fit the
   Programmable Block limits; the commented originals in `Scripts/Source/` are for reading only. The blueprints already carry the scripts in their Programmable Blocks.
2. **Delete the old blueprint folders first.** Open `%AppData%\SpaceEngineers\Blueprints\local\` and remove every folder of an earlier version of these ships (also the `bp.sbcB5` next to
   `bp.sbc`: the game keeps loading that stale cache). This package never ships a `.sbcB5`.
3. Copy the `Blueprints/<Name>` folders you want into `%AppData%\SpaceEngineers\Blueprints\local\`. In game press **F10**, pick the ship and paste it (creative tools, or a projector in survival).
   Every ship is a **dynamic** ship; do not convert it to a station.
4. "In-game scripts" must be enabled in the world settings, otherwise the Programmable Blocks do not run.
5. If something does not paste, send the game log (`%AppData%\SpaceEngineers\SpaceEngineers_*.log`) and say which model and variant. **Which variant?** `<Name>` (Full) uses the whole design,
   including block types whose XML has never been seen in a game-written blueprint (turrets, sensor, AI blocks, decoys, cargo containers, Run toolbar slots); `<Name> Lite` uses only shapes copied
   from a game-written ship (no vanilla turrets on the small ships, so no point defence there, no sensor, no decoys, no toolbar `Run` slots; the Warden and Leviathan Lite keep their rotor turrets, built from the Tech Hunter's own shapes). If a Full ship does not paste, try its Lite twin.
6. Drones for the cradles come from the **Drones** package (Hornet, Wasp, Lancer, Harrier, Aegis, Mantis, Watcher); the `* Wing` ships already carry Hornets.

**Warship specifics.** Large-grid ships are pasted as a free ship in creative mode (or from a projector in survival). The Warden (about 10,300 PCU with its pod) and the Leviathan
(about 33,000 PCU with both pods) need a world limit to match: the repository file `docs/design/ships/Leviathan.md` lists what to delete for a 20,000 PCU world. The pods are separate grids in the same
blueprint, docked by two connector pairs: after the paste look at the hangar connectors in the terminal and press **Lock** on each pair that is not locked. Every ship comes with its
guns loaded, its tanks and batteries full and its Programmable Blocks programmed and configured; there is nothing to copy into a PB. The scripts are in `Scripts/` only for re-pasting.

